{"ratings":[{"id":"C1","consequence":"bypass","trigger":"normal","reason":"The audit blocks PDFs, fonts, audio and video that the request says must pass, which is a false-positive block rather than a bypass, but no listed key fits better than 'wrong' so it is rated as a wrong result that arises in normal operation."},{"id":"C2","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"normal","reason":"Ordinary executable shell scripts are wrongly flagged as binary content and blocked unless Allow: binary is given, and both adjudicators reproduced it."},{"id":"C3","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Valid PNGs with common tEXt, iTXt or iCCP metadata chunks are rejected as opaque media and blocked, which both adjudicators reproduced."},{"id":"C4","consequence":"bypass","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Text containing strings like MZ or ustar is reclassified as binary, and with Allow: binary that text escapes the gitattributes check so -diff rules can hide readable source, which weakens a check the change adds."},{"id":"C5","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"unusual","reason":"Appending to a text file larger than 50 MB hits the subprocess output limit and blocks with an error that no allowance clears, which needs an unusually large file."}]}

Correction: my C1 entry is inconsistent. Its reason says the result is "wrong" but the key I gave was "bypass". The correct C1 rating is:

{"ratings":[{"id":"C1","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"normal","reason":"The audit blocks PDFs, fonts, audio and video that the request says must pass, which is a false-positive block in normal operation."},{"id":"C2","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"normal","reason":"Ordinary executable shell scripts are wrongly flagged as binary content and blocked unless Allow: binary is given, and both adjudicators reproduced it."},{"id":"C3","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Valid PNGs with common tEXt, iTXt or iCCP metadata chunks are rejected as opaque media and blocked, which both adjudicators reproduced."},{"id":"C4","consequence":"bypass","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Text containing strings like MZ or ustar is reclassified as binary, and with Allow: binary that text escapes the gitattributes check so -diff rules can hide readable source, which weakens a check the change adds."},{"id":"C5","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"unusual","reason":"Appending to a text file larger than 50 MB hits the subprocess output limit and blocks with an error that no allowance clears, which needs an unusually large file."}]}
